WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.114 --> 00:00:02.440
(film reeling)

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:04.670
- [Johnny] If you were able to
look through the perspective

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:07.440
of a person who thinks the world is flat,

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.270
you would see this.

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:11.550
The North pole is right
here in the center,

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:14.540
the continent's splayed
out over this plane.

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:19.200
And here on the edges, you'd
run into 150 foot wall of ice,

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.557
guarded by NASA employees with guns.

00:00:21.557 --> 00:00:24.150
- [Recorded Speaker] And how
far that ice goes outwards.

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:25.750
And, when people have
tried to go down there,

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:29.100
they get turned away at
gunpoint and put in prison.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:30.490
- [Johnny] The heavens are a dome

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:32.680
that arcs over the flat earth.

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:34.860
The sun, the moon, the stars,

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:37.500
they're all just little
balls of light in the sky

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:40.373
that move around just
above the earth's surface.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:46.410
There are loads of people
who actually believe this.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:48.960
YouTube channels and Facebook pages.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:51.490
You'll see hundreds of
thousands of followers.

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:54.750
Google searches for the
term flat earth proof

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:56.680
over time look like this.

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:58.620
It's become incredibly popular.

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:01.590
And recently, a poll showed that only 84%

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:03.377
of Americans agree with the statement,

00:01:03.377 --> 00:01:08.120
"I have always believed
the world is round", 84%.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:12.220
And if you're 18 to 24,
that's more like 66%,

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:14.950
which is like dangerously close to half.

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:17.133
What is going on here?

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:19.193
- Now, the North Pole,

00:01:19.193 --> 00:01:21.760
is the center of a deep ocean.

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:23.350
Whereas the South Pole,

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:26.060
is the center of a high plateau,

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:29.030
which averages seven or eight
thousand feet in altitude.

00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:30.140
This is frustrating!

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:31.920
And, what's even more frustrating

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:33.360
is every time I try to look into this

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:35.340
and understand it, all I see is coverage

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:37.630
of like, flat earther conventions

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.632
and like, interviews with these people.

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:42.420
- We absolutely know for
a fact this ain't it.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:43.490
- These interviews are interesting.

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:45.580
but I wanna understand like,

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:47.610
how someone with a thinking brain

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:49.980
can actually get behind this.

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:51.130
What is this actual belief?

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:52.190
Where does it come from?

00:01:52.190 --> 00:01:55.410
And, how do potentially millions of people

00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:57.706
believe that the earth is flat?

00:01:57.706 --> 00:01:59.717
- [Recorded Male Speaker]
The water is completely flat

00:01:59.717 --> 00:02:02.590
as far as we can see and
as far as we've measured,

00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:04.830
and the horizon is completely flat.

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:06.083
- I'm in Mexico now.

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:08.490
I've been sitting on the beach,

00:02:08.490 --> 00:02:11.200
reading everything there is to read

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:14.513
about the history of people
who believe the earth is flat.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:20.930
There's one thing that I
just had to try for myself.

00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:22.550
This is a simple experiment

00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:24.250
that anybody can conduct

00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:27.480
to determine definitely
that the earth is flat.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.518
Grab a spirit level and
take it on a plane with you.

00:02:29.518 --> 00:02:30.530
(speaking Spanish)

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:32.290
- Found this hardware store,

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:33.510
bought myself a level.

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:34.800
Gracias amigo.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:36.430
- One of the stranger
things we've ever done.

00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:38.210
- And I'm bringing it
with me on the airplane.

00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:41.880
I'm gonna do some of this
empirical science myself.

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:45.830
If you are to fly on a non rotating earth,

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:49.550
please explain what kind of experience

00:02:49.550 --> 00:02:51.840
will a pilot really have?

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:53.230
The logic goes

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:56.270
that if the earth is round

00:02:56.270 --> 00:02:58.500
and I'm flying thousands of miles,

00:02:58.500 --> 00:02:59.600
which I'm about to do,

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:02.090
then the airplane will have
to be tipped a little bit

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:03.550
the whole time in order to make it

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:05.040
around the curvature of the earth.

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:08.740
- The plane should be constantly
dipping its nose forward

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:10.620
in order to compensate for the curvature.

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:13.545
- Show me some planes doing this!

00:03:13.545 --> 00:03:15.470
- I would be able to see
the tilt of the airplane.

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:18.090
If I put my newly purchased level

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:19.730
on the tray table in front of me.

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:21.870
- I'm gonna take my spirit
level onto the plane.

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:25.030
- If my tool shows me that
the plane is totally leveled-

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:26.520
- That's proof that the earth is flat.

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:27.920
- Let's go see what happens.

00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:35.420
Can somebody explain to me, duty free?

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:36.520
Why perfume?

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:38.620
Why is there so much perfume in duty free?

00:03:57.050 --> 00:04:00.110
Four hours on an airplane and I'm back.

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:02.850
My little level experiment
worked wonderfully.

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:04.780
The bubble stayed nice and center,

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:07.670
turns out the plane was
not dipping its nose

00:04:07.670 --> 00:04:10.293
in order to (laughs)
make it around the earth.

00:04:10.293 --> 00:04:14.330
This is explained by the
basics of gravity and physics.

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:18.203
This video is not a debunk
of flat earth theory.

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:20.770
That doesn't need to happen!

00:04:20.770 --> 00:04:22.500
That shouldn't need to happen!

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:24.770
What this is, is my fascination

00:04:24.770 --> 00:04:27.070
with the fact that
there is lots of people.

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:27.903
Let's put it this way,

00:04:27.903 --> 00:04:31.070
a non zero number of humans

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:32.950
who think the world is flat!

00:04:32.950 --> 00:04:35.350
And, they work really hard to prove it.

00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:37.280
I wanna understand what sorts of tools

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:41.380
are being used to prove the world is flat.

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:42.734
So, here we go.

00:04:42.734 --> 00:04:45.317
(spacey music)

00:04:49.631 --> 00:04:51.250
I wonder if I can get some really dramatic

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:54.743
like, conspiracy theory
lighting going on here.

00:04:57.032 --> 00:04:57.865
I've seen all the evidence.

00:04:57.865 --> 00:05:00.293
What if the earth actually is flat?

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:05.593
The plane wasn't dipping,
the level was flat.

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:08.433
Okay, I'm kidding!

00:05:08.433 --> 00:05:09.266
Let's get into this.

00:05:09.266 --> 00:05:10.150
I've been in the weeds,

00:05:10.150 --> 00:05:12.980
learning about the flat earth experience,

00:05:12.980 --> 00:05:14.570
what people believe and why,

00:05:14.570 --> 00:05:16.360
and where it all came from.

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:18.033
And, here's what I've learned.

00:05:19.510 --> 00:05:22.720
Number one, flat earthers
have become a thing

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:25.130
just in the past couple hundred years.

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:29.050
So, by like 205 BC, you've
got these really smart

00:05:29.050 --> 00:05:31.940
Greek people making experiments that are

00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:36.110
like, observing a globe shaped earth.

00:05:36.110 --> 00:05:37.820
Over the next several centuries,

00:05:37.820 --> 00:05:40.320
eventually this would just
become the widespread thing

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:44.310
among anyone who was doing
experimentation on the world.

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:47.810
And eventually, nobody
believed the earth was flat.

00:05:47.810 --> 00:05:49.950
Even in like the medieval times.

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:53.630
Like, it was a consensus
that the earth was a globe.

00:05:53.630 --> 00:05:56.490
So in short, flat
earthers, weren't a thing

00:05:56.490 --> 00:05:58.290
during this time, even though literally,

00:05:58.290 --> 00:06:01.460
in elementary school, I was
taught that Christopher Columbus

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:03.950
and like, his voyage was somehow to prove

00:06:03.950 --> 00:06:06.230
that the earth was round
or maybe it was flat.

00:06:06.230 --> 00:06:07.880
And that there was like,
some debate around that.

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:09.370
That's actually a total legend!

00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:11.240
And, I have no idea why I was taught that

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:12.090
in elementary school.

00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:13.090
How did that happen?

00:06:14.090 --> 00:06:16.620
I actually am genuinely curious,
like, how did that happen?

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:19.890
The fact is Christopher
Columbus, the Catholic church,

00:06:19.890 --> 00:06:22.750
the Spanish patrons, no one
thought the earth was flat

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:25.370
but then they became a thing, any sort

00:06:25.370 --> 00:06:28.580
of flat earther movement
didn't actually come around

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:32.663
ironically until science was
really starting to heat up.

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:37.780
During the mid 1800s a huge amount

00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:39.810
of scientific breakthrough was happening.

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:42.070
The scientific method was taking off

00:06:42.070 --> 00:06:44.200
and huge breakthroughs in biology,

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:48.460
physics, anatomy, and
mathematics were taking place.

00:06:48.460 --> 00:06:50.280
But, at the time there were also people

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:53.350
who were becoming
uncomfortable with how advanced

00:06:53.350 --> 00:06:55.083
scientific methods we're getting.

00:06:56.170 --> 00:06:57.617
These guys were like, "Hold on a second.

00:06:57.617 --> 00:07:00.287
"You have all these fancy
new tools to inquire

00:07:00.287 --> 00:07:02.417
"into the world and to understand reality.

00:07:02.417 --> 00:07:04.077
"But, these tools are getting like,

00:07:04.077 --> 00:07:07.367
"too sophisticated and too
abstract and theoretical.

00:07:07.367 --> 00:07:08.707
"They're becoming too disconnected

00:07:08.707 --> 00:07:11.187
"from like, what I can see and understand

00:07:11.187 --> 00:07:12.430
"and touch and feel."

00:07:12.430 --> 00:07:14.170
They wanted to bring science back

00:07:14.170 --> 00:07:16.790
to what it had been
for a really long time,

00:07:16.790 --> 00:07:20.410
which is that like, a person
goes out, uses simple tools

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:22.740
like a telescope to look at the world

00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:26.040
and to make conclusions
about how the world works.

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:27.470
So, it's the 1800s,

00:07:27.470 --> 00:07:29.480
science is like, having it's time.

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:31.410
And, you have these
guys, usually from like,

00:07:31.410 --> 00:07:34.910
the U.S. and the UK who want to throw out

00:07:34.910 --> 00:07:38.830
this growing body of like,
amazing advancements in science.

00:07:38.830 --> 00:07:40.990
And they start to do experiments.

00:07:40.990 --> 00:07:43.063
Here's what those experiments looked like.

00:07:44.374 --> 00:07:47.180
(upbeat music)

00:07:47.180 --> 00:07:49.820
So, it's the summer of 1838,

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:53.270
England up in the County
of Cambridgeshire,

00:07:53.270 --> 00:07:56.180
which literally sounds like a place

00:07:56.180 --> 00:07:57.430
in the Lord of the rings.

00:07:58.670 --> 00:08:00.450
So, it's the summer of 1838.

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:02.690
And, the Atom had just been discovered

00:08:02.690 --> 00:08:05.690
and the Doppler effect is
like, being flushed out.

00:08:05.690 --> 00:08:07.180
And then, you've got this guy,

00:08:07.180 --> 00:08:08.670
his name is Samuel Rowbotham,

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:10.870
but he goes by the pseudonym Parallax,

00:08:10.870 --> 00:08:13.120
which is actually a pretty dope name.

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:14.870
Like, if I were a DJ, I would totally

00:08:14.870 --> 00:08:16.803
go with like, Parallax!

00:08:16.803 --> 00:08:19.240
Anyway, Parallax decides,

00:08:19.240 --> 00:08:21.040
even though all this science is happening,

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:24.000
he thinks it's time to
reopen up the debate

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:26.420
about whether or not the earth is a globe,

00:08:26.420 --> 00:08:29.330
which was like literally settled
thousands of years earlier.

00:08:29.330 --> 00:08:31.220
But he's like, "No, let's do it!"

00:08:31.220 --> 00:08:35.730
And, he finds this canal system
that is incredibly straight.

00:08:35.730 --> 00:08:39.660
This canal goes on for
almost 10 kilometers,

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:42.870
like six miles of just a straight line.

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:44.697
This guy says, "If the earth is a globe

00:08:44.697 --> 00:08:47.547
"and people say it's 25,000
miles in circumference,

00:08:47.547 --> 00:08:49.927
"then if I look at a straight line,

00:08:49.927 --> 00:08:52.827
"after the first mile the
curvature of the earth would mean

00:08:52.827 --> 00:08:55.517
"that the canal would now
be eight inches lower.

00:08:55.517 --> 00:08:58.457
"After two miles, it
would be 32 inches lower.

00:08:58.457 --> 00:09:00.930
"After three miles, 72 inches lower."

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:04.070
Meaning like, six feet,
almost two meters and so on.

00:09:04.070 --> 00:09:06.630
So, he thinks eventually
the dip from the curvature

00:09:06.630 --> 00:09:07.900
of the earth would be so great

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:09.436
that you could easily observe it.

00:09:09.436 --> 00:09:12.186
(puzzling music)

00:09:14.100 --> 00:09:15.640
So, he gets in the water,

00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:17.470
he puts a telescope right above

00:09:17.470 --> 00:09:18.770
the surface of the water

00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:20.660
and then puts a boat on the canal

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:23.100
with a one meter tall post on it.

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:24.660
So, what he wants to see is

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:26.960
if the earth is curved, if it's a globe,

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:30.410
this post will start to
disappear over the horizon.

00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:31.780
So, he does it.

00:09:31.780 --> 00:09:33.240
The boat goes away.

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:35.470
It goes the entire six miles

00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:39.990
of the canal and it stays
in sight the entire time.

00:09:39.990 --> 00:09:41.873
It doesn't dip over the horizon.

00:09:43.410 --> 00:09:44.370
And, he's stoked!

00:09:44.370 --> 00:09:48.377
He's like, "Man, I just
proved that the earth is flat.

00:09:48.377 --> 00:09:50.560
"And I did it with a
telescope and a boat."

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:51.900
Like, screw you science!

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:54.970
Like, I'm making breakthroughs
right here in Cambridgeshire!

00:09:54.970 --> 00:09:56.490
And then, he writes this book,

00:09:56.490 --> 00:09:58.010
where he flushes out this experiment

00:09:58.010 --> 00:09:59.630
and several others that he does.

00:09:59.630 --> 00:10:01.560
But wait, this experiment's like,

00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:03.270
kind of legit, right?

00:10:03.270 --> 00:10:05.640
It adds up, like his
numbers were all correct

00:10:05.640 --> 00:10:08.140
about the circumference
and the dip of a curvature.

00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:09.100
Like, why didn't it dip?

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:11.260
Like, why was the boat still in sight?

00:10:11.260 --> 00:10:12.880
There's nothing wrong
with this experiment.

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:15.070
Parallax, got that great name!

00:10:15.070 --> 00:10:16.520
Maybe he was on to something!

00:10:19.705 --> 00:10:20.538
(beep)

00:10:20.538 --> 00:10:21.880
No, no, this is stupid!

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:24.000
This is like a third
grade science experiment

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:24.960
in your backyard!

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:26.460
This experiment doesn't take into account

00:10:26.460 --> 00:10:28.620
how the natural world actually works

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:29.820
and how light behaves

00:10:29.820 --> 00:10:33.050
and refracts based on the
different air densities!

00:10:33.050 --> 00:10:35.270
This is like stuff that
people already figured out.

00:10:35.270 --> 00:10:37.410
And like, Parallax is
sitting there getting wet

00:10:37.410 --> 00:10:41.470
in a canal, like trying
to observe this on.

00:10:41.470 --> 00:10:43.500
No, this does not prove anything!

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:45.750
But Parallax didn't
wanna hear any of this.

00:10:45.750 --> 00:10:48.680
He didn't wanna talk about
atmospheric refraction

00:10:48.680 --> 00:10:51.940
and air density and how light
behaves in different media.

00:10:51.940 --> 00:10:54.390
Too complicated, too abstract.

00:10:54.390 --> 00:10:56.450
You can't touch and feel that stuff.

00:10:56.450 --> 00:11:00.280
Instead, Parallax sees
science and observing reality

00:11:00.280 --> 00:11:02.020
as a much simpler task.

00:11:02.020 --> 00:11:04.357
In his book, he says, "Nature speaks to us

00:11:04.357 --> 00:11:07.667
"in a peculiar language, in
the language of phenomenon.

00:11:07.667 --> 00:11:10.710
"She answers at all times the questions

00:11:10.710 --> 00:11:12.140
which are put to her."

00:11:12.140 --> 00:11:13.240
Just like, go out and like,

00:11:13.240 --> 00:11:15.800
put a question to mother
nature and she'll answer it.

00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:18.550
As scientific methods
become more sophisticated,

00:11:18.550 --> 00:11:20.720
they become harder for
you and me to understand.

00:11:20.720 --> 00:11:22.680
Parallax and his canal experiments are

00:11:22.680 --> 00:11:24.170
a reaction to all of this.

00:11:24.170 --> 00:11:27.100
They are a call for a simplification

00:11:27.100 --> 00:11:30.380
of scientific methods and
to return of the senses

00:11:30.380 --> 00:11:32.650
as the primary force for
understanding reality.

00:11:32.650 --> 00:11:36.150
He called his method of
reductionist pseudoscience

00:11:36.150 --> 00:11:37.580
the Zetetic method.

00:11:37.580 --> 00:11:39.400
He says that honesty of thought

00:11:39.400 --> 00:11:41.510
is to look at truth in the face,

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:44.420
not the side face, but the full front.

00:11:44.420 --> 00:11:45.500
Like, just like look at it,

00:11:45.500 --> 00:11:47.230
go out and observe it for yourself.

00:11:47.230 --> 00:11:48.950
He was among several scientists

00:11:48.950 --> 00:11:50.820
and mathematicians at the time

00:11:50.820 --> 00:11:52.860
who were on this train of

00:11:52.860 --> 00:11:56.280
let's use really simplified reductionist

00:11:56.280 --> 00:11:58.680
math and science to prove that

00:11:58.680 --> 00:11:59.970
the earth is actually flat.

