00:15:44.490 --> 00:15:47.280
Instead, we read about this stuff.

00:15:47.280 --> 00:15:49.200
We benefit from its findings.

00:15:49.200 --> 00:15:51.330
We pay our taxes to fund more of it.

00:15:51.330 --> 00:15:53.530
Science is like a tall tower

00:15:53.530 --> 00:15:55.880
and each individual
researcher and institution

00:15:55.880 --> 00:15:57.500
adds a little brick to that tower.

00:15:57.500 --> 00:15:59.560
Each brick resting on the one below it.

00:15:59.560 --> 00:16:03.180
No one person sees or
understands all of the bricks.

00:16:03.180 --> 00:16:05.460
Instead, we have a system of debate,

00:16:05.460 --> 00:16:07.520
reviews, scrutiny that only allows

00:16:07.520 --> 00:16:10.270
the most accurate information
to be added to the tower.

00:16:11.690 --> 00:16:14.340
And honestly, I don't think
humans are well suited

00:16:14.340 --> 00:16:17.300
to adapt to this very impersonal way

00:16:17.300 --> 00:16:18.420
of understanding the world.

00:16:18.420 --> 00:16:21.010
We have evolved over millions of years

00:16:21.010 --> 00:16:23.920
with our senses as our
main driver of survival.

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:27.530
And now, we live in a society
that is run by big systems

00:16:27.530 --> 00:16:31.070
and impersonal institutions
that we will never touch

00:16:31.070 --> 00:16:33.450
and feel, much less understand.

00:16:33.450 --> 00:16:36.840
And that's why we have people
who believe the world is flat,

00:16:36.840 --> 00:16:40.330
